# Conventional Commits

Source: [git-conventional-commit-messages](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

## Format
```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

## Types
- `feat` — new feature
- `fix` — bug fix
- `refactor` — code change without behavior change
- `perf` — performance improvement
- `test` — tests only
- `docs` — documentation
- `chore` — tooling, deps, CI
- `style` — formatting only (no logic change)

## Scope examples (ARTSA)
- `frontend`, `backend`, `containment`, `api`, `observatory`, `deps`

## Rules
- Description imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period: `feat(frontend): wire observatory to live API`
- Breaking changes: `feat(api)!: rename ingest payload field` or footer `BREAKING CHANGE: ...`
- One logical change per commit; don't mix frontend redesign with backend refactors
